- Report which tests pass before finishing.

## SECURITY REQUIREMENTS
- Notifications, profiles, wallets, merchant data and lender data are private to their owner. Enforce on the backend with row-level rules (Firebase Security Rules or Supabase RLS, whichever the project already uses).
- Subscription limits (including the KES 250 tier), the 30-day expiry, the upgrade-only-after-expiry rule, verification checks, exemptions, the shop visit requirement, subscription and featured fees, and "only the merchant can add groups and the group icon, only in their own products" must all be enforced server-side. Never trust values sent from the client.
- A merchant has no authority over a group after creating it: no edit, no delete, no control. Enforce on the server and in the rules.
- Group chat is private to the group and the product's merchant. Moderation runs on the server before delivery, and warnings, mutes and blacklists are enforced on the server.
- Only admins can approve or decline subscriptions, featured payments, coin acceptance, verification, shop visit results and exemptions (whole or part, with a valid reason), and confirm or reverse chat blacklists.
- Wallet transfers (for both subscription and featured payments) must be atomic: the debit and credit succeed together or neither happens. Prevent double payments and negative balances.
- Group capacity must be enforced server-side so a group can never exceed its speed, even when two members join at the same moment.
- Do not expose private data of one merchant, member or lender to another.

## ACCEPTANCE TESTS
1. The header no longer contains Notifications. Each user (member, merchant, lender) has a private Notification section in their profile.
2. Every user has a profile. A member's profile has Overview, Personal Details, Address Book, Orders, My Groups, Saved Items, Followed Merchants, Recently Viewed, Notifications, Wallet link and Account Settings, in a familiar Jumia-style layout.
3. There is no cart, "Add to cart" button, cart icon or cart page anywhere in the app. Members purchase only through groups.
4. User A cannot see User B's notifications or profile data, even by changing an ID in the URL.
5. An admin broadcast (for example, a maintenance notice) appears in every user's notifications.
6. A merchant cannot post products or create groups unless registered, verified and subscribed for the current 30 days.
7. A merchant cannot be verified unless every requirement is met or exempted: physical shop, uploaded trading licence, ID or passport number, more than 3 years of operation, and the Buyoll shop visit. Only an admin can exempt the whole set or any part of it, and only with a written reason. An exemption without a reason is rejected by the backend, and every exemption appears in the audit log.
8. The admin Merchant Verification section lets an admin schedule and record the shop visit, confirm the "Buyoll Verified Merchant" advert installation, grant exemptions and verify or decline. After verification the merchant shows the "Buyoll Verified Merchant" badge, and a merchant who is not verified does not.
9. Each tier enforces its limits: 250: 2 products max and 2 groups per product; 500: 10 products and 5 groups; 1,500: 50 and 10; 3,500: 100 and 30; 7,500: unlimited products and 50 groups; Enterprise: custom, up to 100 groups per product. Expiry on day 31 blocks posting.
10. A KES 250 merchant cannot post a 3rd product or add a 3rd group to a product, even by calling the backend directly.
11. A product posted to Announcements is free. A featured product costs KES 30 per day.
12. Paying the featured fee with wallet coins debits the merchant, credits the admin wallet and updates both balances automatically, with the reason recorded as "featured product".
13. Paying the subscription fee with wallet coins debits the merchant, credits the admin wallet and updates both balances automatically, with the reason recorded as "subscription", and the 30-day subscription starts.
14. A manual till/paybill payment (for a subscription or a featured product) with code, amount and reason is held until an admin approves or declines it. The subscription or featured period starts only after approval.
15. Admin has working Merchant Verification, Featured Products, Subscriptions, Coins Acceptance and Chat Moderation sections.
16. An approved featured product appears in Featured for exactly the paid period and also in Announcements.
17. Only the merchant who created a product sees "Add group" and the group icon option inside it. They choose the speed (1 to 10), and the button stops working once the tier limit is reached. Other users and other merchants never see it.
18. Groups created by the merchant are visible to all users, including new users, inside the product.
19. After creating a group, the merchant sees no edit, delete, deactivate or manage option on it. A direct backend request from the merchant to edit or delete a group (including its speed or icon) is rejected.
20. The merchant can notify and chat with a group, and nothing else.
21. A member can join more than one group (in the same product and across products), all of them appear in My Groups, and a full group cannot accept more members.
22. A member can pick any group, invite friends, and the first person to invite becomes the group moderator.
23. A chat message from a group (moderator) to the merchant appears in the merchant's notifications with the group name, product, preview and a link. Tapping the link opens that group in view-only mode, and the merchant can tap "Reply" to respond in the chat.
24. The merchant and the group moderator can chat in both directions in real time. Other merchants and people outside the group cannot see or send messages, even by guessing a URL or ID.
25. A message with insults or defamatory language is censored or blocked by the platform before delivery, a platform warning is sent to the culprit, and the incident appears in the admin Chat Moderation section.
26. Repeat violations escalate from warning to temporary mute to chat blacklist. A muted or blacklisted user cannot send messages, even by calling the backend directly, and sees a clear notice and appeal option.
27. The Merchant section has an Upgrade feature. While the subscription is active, Upgrade is disabled and shows the end date, and the backend rejects any upgrade attempt before the subscription ends.
28. After the subscription ends, tapping Upgrade shows all plans with their amounts and benefits. The merchant picks one, pays (wallet coins or manual), and once payment is confirmed the plan activates automatically with new limits and a fresh 30-day period.
29. After upgrading from a lower plan, the merchant can immediately post more products and create more groups per product, according to the new plan.
30. Enterprise cannot be paid until an admin sets its price and limits for that merchant.
31. Only one subscription payment can be pending at a time, and every plan change appears in the subscription history.
32. The backend passes automated tests for plan limits, upgrade-only-after-expiry, verification and exemptions, atomic wallet transfers, idempotent payments, group capacity races, merchant group immutability, chat access control, chat moderation and data isolation between users.
33. The login/sign up model is unchanged, and all previously working features still work (no regressions).
